+# U10 GT9XX resource port checkpoint — 2026-09-28
+
+Category: **PROPER-FIX**, source resource wiring only; default off.
+
+## Hypothesis and evidence
+
+FACT: existing GT9XX_MZ is the m681 port. Its OF table only accepts
+`mediatek,cap_touch`, and its GPIO/power macros use raw GPIO10/GPIO1 and MT6351
+registers 0x0aa2/0x0aa4. U10 needs its own resource profile. Adding just a
+compatible would bind a driver with the wrong PMIC implementation.
+
+FACT: exact stock U10 `kernel.decompressed` SHA256
+`adb5309dade5477ae11aeae58436ff234cdb88be590685af8d06d14c9ea51748`,
+boot SHA256 `03bde51ce54248ac380d47adf8f37bc8a3de374b480a5bc9ef2d536682538188`,
+DTB SHA256 `07e70460413b8be2bad6a0d0c3acb81017d7c2550cea9fed397cccd50df1d00f`.
+Recovered own kallsyms/ELF base is `ffffffc000080000`, checked against raw bytes.
+This is not a donor System.map and no runtime image was flashed.
+
+Real Ghidra MCP receipts, private durable directory
+`/home/n8n/cloud_oss_builds/kernel-reverse/20260928/`:
+
+| Receipt | Stock address and fact |
+|---|---|
+| u10-tpd-local-init-decompile-mcp.json | ffffffc000815c60: regulator_get(vtouch), set_voltage(2800000,3300000) before driver registration |
+| u10-tpd-power-on-decompile-mcp.json | ffffffc000817778: INT0, RST0, 20ms, pmic_ldo_vldo28_sw_en(1), reset20, I2C test; four attempts |
+| u10-gtp-reset-guitar-decompile-mcp.json | ffffffc0008168ac: logical RST0/INT1 pinctrl, address strap, 2ms/6ms/50ms waits |
+| u10-tpd-gpio-output-decompile-mcp.json | ffffffc00080a684: pinctrl state selection, not raw GPIO writes |
+| u10-force-reset-guitar-decompile-mcp.json | ffffffc000817e14: named VLDO28 off/on with 30ms waits |
+
+FACT: `gt9xx_dt_match` at ffffffc000c00900 has only
+`mediatek,cap_touch_gt`, matched to U10 DT i2c0@0x5d; FocalTech has its own
+`mediatek,cap_touch` at 0x38. DT touch IRQ=1 falling, reset pad10, INT pad1,
+vtouch resolves to ldo_vldo28. An attached unit's actual touch vendor is unknown.
+
+## Files and purpose
+
+- `drivers/input/touchscreen/mediatek/Kconfig`: explicit default-n U10 profile,
+  dependent on GT9XX_MZ, OF, regulator support and built-in MT6353.
+- `GT9XX_MZ/Makefile`: MT6353 API header path only for that profile.
+- `GT9XX_MZ/tpd_custom_gt9xx.h`: logical pinctrl and named PMIC API macros;
+  retains original CRLF and the old m681 resource branch.
+- `GT9XX_MZ/gt9xx_driver.c`: exact U10 OF identity, voltage preparation,
+  bounded stock first-probe ordering, error and resource cleanup.
+
+The API owner is `pmic/mt6353/pmic_api_ldo.c:820`: it writes the named
+VLDO28_EN_0/EN_1 fields. PMIC Makefiles select that object with MT6353.
+No regulator_enable call is substituted for the observed U10 API. U20 uses
+regulator_enable in its own stock and M3s uses legacy hwPowerOn; this profile
+must not be enabled for either board.
+
+## Validation, expected marker, rollback
+
+FACT: only source/preprocessor checks have run. Default profile produces the
+same preprocessed tokens as base `693b6a4d81e17e06545a4329064d5d01cd912060`.
+U10 preprocessing confirms its distinct OF table, no raw m681 register calls,
+four attempts, logical pins, named rail API and errno/cleanup branches.
+No C compilation, kernel build, DTB build, boot image, flash or runtime proof.
+
+Expected next marker after the remaining gates and an authorized test:
+I2C 0-005d bound to gt9xx, successful version read, own board configuration,
+then IRQ1 activity and calibrated input. This checkpoint alone does not assert
+those outcomes. Revert this checkpoint if default profile token equivalence
+breaks or a stock/reference comparison disproves the selected resource path.
+
+Verification from the fleet export directory:
+`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 tools/validate_u10_profile.py kernel-checkout`
+`git -C kernel-checkout -c core.whitespace=cr-at-eol diff --check`
+
+## Blocking gates before enabling
+
+FACT: no defconfig enables the new option. Own U10 DTS/DCT has not been wired
+into this source base. Existing donor `GTP_CUSTOM_CFG=1`, `GTP_AUTO_UPDATE=1`
+and selected firmware/config tables are not U10-proven. They must be resolved
+from own stock or verified source before enabling this resource profile.
+FT/Goodix dual-source linking, panel selection, regulator registration, callback
+configuration, gestures/suspend and input calibration remain separate gates.
+Do not turn this source checkpoint into a ready target or a flash candidate.
